<Docs title="Compatibility policy" description="AgentGuard versioning, runtime, and support boundaries.">
  <div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">PROJECT / COMPATIBILITY</span><h1>Know the support contract.</h1><p>Compatibility is specific to a surface. Library primitives do not automatically become standalone server features.</p></div>
  <h2>Supported baseline</h2><div class="docs-table"><div><b>Rust</b><span>MSRV 1.89, enforced in CI. The workspace is tested on stable and the declared MSRV.</span></div><div><b>Node.js</b><span>Node.js 20.9+; CI and release images use Node 22.19.0 with pnpm 11.22.0.</span></div><div><b>Deployment</b><span>Docker images deployed to Kubernetes are the supported production reference topology.</span></div><div><b>Interfaces</b><span>Rust library, CLI, TypeScript subprocess SDK, AuthZEN HTTP PDP, and repository-defined plaintext loopback gRPC.</span></div></div>
  <h2>Versioning and changes</h2><p>Crate and package versions follow the repository release. Breaking API, policy, token, or configuration changes require a changelog entry and migration guidance. Deprecated surfaces remain documented until their removal release; security fixes target the latest release.</p>
  <p>Read the versioned <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/docs/compatibility.md">compatibility policy ↗</a> and <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/SUPPORT.md">support policy ↗</a>.</p>
</Docs>
